{title: How Great Thou Art}
{key: B}

{comment: Verse 1}
O Lord my [G]God, When I in [C/G]awesome wonder,
Consider [G]all the Worlds Thy [D/Gb]hand hath [G]made.
I see the [G]stars, I hear the [C/G]rolling thunder
Thy pow'r through[G]out the uni[D/Gb]verse dis[G]played

{comment: Chorus}
Then sings my [G]soul, my [C/G]Savior God, to [G]Thee
How great Thou [Am7]art! How great Thou [G]art!
Then sings my soul, my [C/G]Savior God, to [G]Thee
How great Thou [Am7]art! How [C/G]great Thou [G]art!

{comment: Verse 2}
When Christ shall [G]come, with shouts of ac[C/G]clamation
And take me [G]home, what joy shall [D/Gb]fill my  [G]heart
Then I shall [G]bow in humble a[C/G]doration
And there pro[G]claim, My God, how [D/Gb]great You [G]are!

{comment: Verse 3}
And when I [G]think that God, His [C/G]Son not sparing
Sent Him to [G]die, I scarce can [D/Gb]take it  [G]in
That on the [G]cross, my burden gladly [C/G]bearing
He bled and [G]died to take a[D/Gb]way  my  [G]sin
